-- title:
--   Regular special fibre at a good point of the two-chart model (q=2)
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime with $q=2$, and $M'$ is a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lying over $q$, in the sense that $q$ is a non-unit of $A$ (`LiesOverPrime`). Write $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ for its residue field, $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A, M')$ for the intermediate field of $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$-Laurent series generated by the two $j$-expansions $j(q)$ and $j(q^{M'})$, and $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$, $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ for the base changes to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the full level-$M'$ modular function field and of the function field of level $q^2M'$ attached to $\mathrm{levelH}\,q\,M'$, the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/q)^\times$. Here a *place* of a field extension $F/K$ is a valuation subring of $F$ containing the image of $K$, distinct from $F$ and with principal ideals; `ord`, `evalAt`, `IsRational` are the associated order function, the evaluation of a function at a rational place, and the condition that $K$ maps onto the residue field.
--
--   **Supersingular places and the constant reduction.** $W$ is a finite set of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A, M')$ over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$, and `hW` says that $W$ consists exactly of the supersingular places $\mathrm{ssPlaces}\,q\,M'$, i.e. the rational affine geometric places at which the geometric $j$-invariant takes a value in $\mathrm{ssJSet}\,q$ (those $j$ for which every elliptic curve with that invariant has no nonzero $q$-torsion point). The hypothesis `hle` asserts $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M' \le \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$. Further, $R_0$ is a `ConstantReduction` of $A$ on $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ with values in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A, M')$: a valuation subring $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ whose intersection with $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is $A$, a surjective residue homomorphism with kernel the maximal ideal, compatible with reduction on constants, a scaling clause making every nonzero function have nonzero reduction after multiplication by a constant, and a place map preserving degrees and compatible with orders of divisors. The hypothesis `hR₀` states that for a Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-Laurent series lies in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$, that element lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and its $R_0$-residue is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$.
--
--   **Igusa and supersingular valuation rings.** $\zeta$ is an element of $\mathrm{Idx}\,q$, i.e. a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$; $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ assigns a valuation subring of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ to each point of the projective line $\mathbb P^1(\mathbb Z/q)$, and $O_{\mathrm{SS}}$ one to each element of $W$. The hypotheses on them are: `hIg_inf`, that $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\mathrm{lineInfty}\,q)$ is the Gauss ring, $f$ belonging to it precisely when $f\cdot y = x$ for Laurent series $x,y$ over $A$ with $y$ having nonzero coefficientwise reduction; `hIg`, that every line $\ell$ is $\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma \cdot \mathrm{lineInfty}\,q$ for some $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ with $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ the pullback of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\mathrm{lineInfty}\,q)$ along $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma$; `hIg_inj`, injectivity of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$; and `hIg_perm`, that for every $\zeta'$ and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ pullback along $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta'\,\gamma$ permutes the family $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$. For $O_{\mathrm{SS}}$: `hSS_A` says each $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ meets the constants in $A$; `hSS_over` says that for $s \in W$ and $f \in R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ which has nonnegative order at every place of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ at which the modular invariant $j$ (the image of $\mathrm{jq}$ under $\mathrm{coeffEmb}$) has nonnegative order, if the $R_0$-residue of $f$ lies in the valuation subring of $s$ then the image of $f$ in $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$, and for every $a \in A$ whose residue equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of that $R_0$-residue the difference of $f$ and $a$ lies in the maximal ideal of $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$; `hSS_fix` says each $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ is invariant under pullback along $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta'\,\gamma$ for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; `hSS_tr` provides for each $s$ an element $t \in O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ such that $t-a$ is a unit of $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ for every $a \in A$.
--
--   **The Drinfeld-level prolongation.** $R$ is a `RegularProlongation` of $A$ on $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ with values in $\mathrm{xHFunctionFieldC}(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A, q^2M', \mathrm{levelH}\,q\,M')$ — a valuation subring with surjective residue map of kernel the maximal ideal, inducing $A$ on constants, reducing constants correctly and satisfying the scaling clause — subject to `hR`, $R.\mathrm{integers} = O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\mathrm{lineInfty}\,q)$, and `hR₀O`, that $f \in R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ if and only if its image in $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\mathrm{lineInfty}\,q)$.
--
--   **Constants.** $\pi \in \overline{\mathbb Q}$ satisfies $\pi^{q^2-1} = q$ and lies in $A$. Next, $k_0$ is an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ and $\pi_0 \in k_0$ lies in $A$; the hypotheses `hdvr`, `hunif`, `hhens`, `hres`, `hκ` state respectively that $A \cap k_0$ is a discrete valuation ring, that its maximal ideal is generated by $\pi_0$, that it is henselian, that its residue field is algebraically closed, and that every element of $A$ agrees, modulo the maximal ideal of $A$, with an element of $k_0 \cap A$. Then $\ell$ is a prime with $\ell \ge 3$, $\ell \ne q$, $\ell \nmid M'$; $\zeta_0 \in k_0$ is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity; $\varpi_t \in k_0$ lies in $A$ and satisfies $\varpi_t^{q^2-1} = q u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$. Finally $K_1$ is a finite extension of $k_0$ inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and $A_1$ a valuation subring of $K_1$ cut out by $A$ (hypothesis `hA₁`), assumed to be a henselian discrete valuation ring.
--
--   **The geometric frame.** $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ is regarded as a $k_0$-algebra through $\overline{\mathbb Q}$. The assertion is made for every intermediate field $F_0$ of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ over $k_0$ satisfying four conditions: the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ together with $F_0$ is all of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$; $F_0$ is stable under every $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta'\,\gamma$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; a linear disjointness clause, namely that for every finite extension $K'/k_0$ in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, every $m$, every $c : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$ linearly independent over $K'$ and every family $a$ of elements of the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K'$ together with $F_0$, the vanishing of $\sum_i c_i a_i$ forces all $a_i = 0$; and that $F_0$ contains every element of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ whose Laurent series has rational coefficients, i.e. lies in the range of $\mathrm{coeffEmb}$.
--
--   Put $T_1 := \mathrm{adjoin}_{k_0}(\text{image of } K_1) \sqcup F_0$, the $k_0$-subfield of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ generated by the image of $K_1$ and $F_0$. An $A_1$-algebra structure on $T_1$ is given, assumed compatible with the inclusions of $A_1 \subseteq K_1$ and of $K_1$ into $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$, and $j_1 \in T_1$ is assumed to have as image in $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ the modular invariant, the inclusion of the element of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ given by $\mathrm{coeffEmb}\,\mathrm{jq}$, with $j_1 \ne 0$. The scheme in question is the two-chart integral model $\mathfrak X_1 := \mathrm{TwoChartIntegralModel}\,A_1\,T_1\,j_1$, the pushout glueing $X_{\mathrm{Fin}} = \mathrm{Spec}\,\mathrm{chartAlgFin}$ and $X_{\mathrm{Inf}} = \mathrm{Spec}\,\mathrm{chartAlgInf}$, where $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}$ (resp. $\mathrm{chartAlgInf}$) is the subalgebra of elements of $T_1$ integral over $A_1[j_1]$ (resp. over $A_1[j_1^{-1}]$), with structure morphism $\mathrm{toBase}$ to $\mathrm{Spec}\,A_1$ and chart immersions $\iota_{\mathrm{Fin}}$, $\iota_{\mathrm{Inf}}$.
--
--   **Auxiliary predicates.** The statement introduces five local definitions. For a point $x$ of $\mathfrak X_1$ and $f \in T_1$: $\mathrm{InStalk}\,x\,f$ holds when, for every point $y$ of $X_{\mathrm{Fin}}$ with $\iota_{\mathrm{Fin}}(y) = x$, there are $g,h \in \mathrm{chartAlgFin}$ with $h \notin y$ and $fh = g$ in $T_1$, and likewise on the $X_{\mathrm{Inf}}$ chart; $\mathrm{InMax}\,x\,f$ is the same with the extra requirement $g \in y$ on both charts. For a place $P$ of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, $\mathrm{Centred}\,P\,x$ holds when $P$ is rational and every $f$ with $\mathrm{InStalk}\,x\,f$ lies in the valuation subring of $P$, has $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f) \in A$, and satisfies $A$-valuation of $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)$ less than $1$ if and only if $\mathrm{InMax}\,x\,f$. $\mathrm{GoodPt}\,x$ is the conjunction of five clauses: $\mathrm{toBase}$ sends $x$ to the closed point of $\mathrm{Spec}\,A_1$; $x$ specialises only to itself; on each chart, every chart element whose image in $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ is a non-unit of $R.\mathrm{integers}$ lies in the prime $y$ for every $y$ over $x$; and for every $y$ of $X_{\mathrm{Fin}}$ over $x$, every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}$ to $\Omega$ with kernel $y$, the value $\varphi(\mathrm{jChartFin})$ is not in $\mathrm{ssJSet}\,q\,\Omega$. For a place $Q$ of $\mathrm{xHFunctionFieldC}(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A, q^2M', \mathrm{levelH}\,q\,M')$, $\mathrm{Reads}\,x\,Q$ holds when every $f$ with $\mathrm{InStalk}\,x\,f$ lies in $R.\mathrm{integers}$, has $R$-residue in the valuation subring of $Q$, and this residue is a non-unit there exactly when $\mathrm{InMax}\,x\,f$. Finally $\mathrm{OffBranch}\,x$ requires that for every line $\ell \ne \mathrm{lineInfty}\,q$ and every $y$ over $x$ on either chart there is a chart element whose image is a non-unit of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ and which does not lie in $y$. Of these, only $\mathrm{GoodPt}$ occurs in the conclusion; $\mathrm{Centred}$, $\mathrm{Reads}$ and $\mathrm{OffBranch}$ are bound so that the statement carries the same frame as its companions.
--
--   **Conclusion.** For every point $x$ of $\mathfrak X_1$ with $\mathrm{GoodPt}\,x$, every $\varpi_1 \in A_1$ generating the maximal ideal of $A_1$, and every element $\varpi_x$ of the stalk of $\mathfrak X_1$ at $x$ which is the germ at $x$ of the global section obtained from $\varpi_1$ by the isomorphism $\Gamma \circ \mathrm{Spec} \cong \mathrm{id}$ for $A_1$ followed by $\mathrm{toBase}$ on global sections, the quotient of the stalk $\mathcal O_{\mathfrak X_1,x}$ by the ideal generated by $\varpi_x$ is a regular local ring.
--
--   This is the regularity of the special fibre of the two-chart integral model $\mathfrak X_1$ of the level-$q^2M'$ modular function field at a good closed point — one lying on the $\infty$-branch determined by the Gauss prolongation $R$ and over an ordinary $j$-invariant — in the case $q = 2$, the companion of the corresponding statement for $q \ge 5$. It is used in the construction of the semistable covering along the Igusa leg, being cited by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.eq_of_reads_of_reads_of_goodPt_twoChartIntegralModel_of_eq_two`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.eq_of_reads_of_reads_of_goodPt_twoChartIntegralModel_of_eq_two) and [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.offBranch_of_goodPt_twoChartIntegralModel_of_eq_two`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.offBranch_of_goodPt_twoChartIntegralModel_of_eq_two).
